  "title": "Michael C Probable NDE 4939",
  "date": "1978",
  "content": "I was in surgery for a cervical fusion from a broken neck several months prior. I remember the doctor counting me backwards from a hundred not very far like ninety-four or something. Then I felt cold air bellowing my gown and I was in a very dark place floating. Looking down I saw myself in a hospital gown lying on a ping-pong table (I played ping-pong a lot back then). The area around the table and me was very bright but all else was darkness, it was like a circle of bright light with the table me and some doctors and nurses doing something to me. I remember I could hear my dad saying everything was going to be all right. Then all of a sudden, I was falling towards the table, it seemed very far away but I was falling very fast almost instantaneous and then I hit and actually felt like I fell and landed hard. I didn't see anything after that but a heard a man yelling at me saying, 'Mike stay with us! Come on Mike!' Then it felt like someone had a hook inside my throat and around the back of my neck and they pulled it real hard. The next thing I remember was coming to in recovery.",
